# Code quality

## Design

- One responsibility per module/class/method.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Prefer immutable `@dataclass(frozen=True)` value objects for cohesive parameter groups.
- Ordinary public methods: prefer ≤5 parameters excluding `self`/`cls`.
- Prefer methods ≤40–50 logical lines; modules preferably below ~400 lines.
- Prefer cyclomatic complexity ≤10 for ordinary methods.
- Guard clauses over deep nesting. No speculative factories or unused abstractions.

## Refactors

- Behavior-preserving by default.
- Never bypass security boundaries, Owner gates, credential redaction, or deny-by-default network policy to “simplify” code.
- Keep synthetic vs real evidence classes distinct.
- Do not enable live Cursor ACP, real Podman, or real credentials in automation.

## Testing

- Add or update tests when changing business logic.
- Architecture regression tests must keep failing on new layer violations.
- Do not invent PASS without executed evidence.
